/*
:name: spec_lexical_str_escape_u_range
:type: error
:error: invalid escape
*/
// docs 02-basics "Strings": "`\u{N}`: Unicode character UTF-8 encoded, 1 to 6
// hexadecimal digits"; qa.md Q41/appendix 8 adopt the Rust set ("`\u{1..6
// hex}`"), where a code point above 10FFFF is an error. 110000 is not a Unicode
// character, so the escape must be rejected (today it is accepted and the string
// silently holds the 10 raw characters `\u{110000}`).
const s = "\u{110000}"   // locate_error_here
